======================================================================================================================
ITEM 99 -- the Local Sheet's cold flow, and how much braking mass it allows
======================================================================================================================

----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
PART A -- the local Hubble diagram from the Updated Nearby Galaxy Catalog
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  UNGC loaded: 869 galaxies; distance methods TRGB 272, Cep 20, TF 204, mem 170, SBF 25
  selection declared up front, and it is Karachentsev's own: TRGB or Cepheid distance, tidal index Theta_1 < 0 (not dominated by a nearer group), 0.7 < D_LG < 3 Mpc  ->  23 galaxies
  straight-line fit: V_LG = 110.2 D -96.7 km/s, scatter 34.1 km/s, and the line crosses zero at R0 = 0.88 Mpc
  the apparent local expansion rate, 110 km/s/Mpc, is far above the cosmic 67 -- that is not a Hubble tension, it is the Local Group braking the nearby flow, and it is the signal
  bootstrap uncertainty on the measured zero-velocity radius: R0 = 0.88 +- 0.15 Mpc (4000 of 4000 resamples usable)
  [PASS] 99a the flow IS cold and the deceleration IS there: a few tens of km/s of scatter about a line whose zero crossing sits near 0.9 Mpc, which is where the Local Group's zero-velocity surface has been measured for two decades   (N = 23, scatter 34.1 km/s, R0(linear) = 0.88 Mpc, apparent H0_local = 110 km/s/Mpc)

----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
PART B -- integrating the flow from z = 50 to today, three ways
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  flat LambdaCDM background from the same Planck parameters the rest of the repository uses: Omega_m = 0.3134, Omega_L = 0.6866, H0 = 67.4  ->  age 13.82 Gyr
  [PASS] 99b the integrator is CORRECT: with the group's mass set to zero it reproduces the unperturbed background exactly -- the test particle ends at the radius it started from in comoving terms and moves at exactly H0 times that radius.  A sign error in the background term or in Lambda cannot pass this   (target r = 2.000 Mpc, got 2.0000; v = 134.80 km/s against H0 r = 134.80)
